@[expose] public section

/-!
# Regular quotients of regular local rings

@stack 00NR
-/

/- Lemma 10.106.4: if `R` and `R ⧸ I` are regular local rings, then `I` is the
parameter ideal of a family which extends to a regular system of parameters of `R`.
Equivalently, `I` is generated by an initial segment of a minimal generating set of
the maximal ideal. -/
@[stacks 00NR]
#check @IsRegularLocalRing.exists_parameterIdeal_eq_of_quotient

/- The pairwise reusable form characterizes regular-local quotients by such parameter
ideals. -/
@[stacks 00NR "parameter-ideal quotient criterion"]
#check @IsRegularLocalRing.quotient_iff_exists_parameterIdeal
